  49:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** File    : SEGGER_RTT.c
  50:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Purpose : Implementation of SEGGER real-time transfer (RTT) which
  51:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           allows real-time communication on targets which support
  52:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           debugger memory accesses while the CPU is running.
  53:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Revision: $Rev: 29668 $
  54:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  55:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Additional information:
  56:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Type "int" is assumed to be 32-bits in size
  57:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           H->T    Host to target communication
  58:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           T->H    Target to host communication
  59:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  60:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           RTT channel 0 is always present and reserved for Terminal usage.
  61:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Name is fixed to "Terminal"
  62:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  63:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Effective buffer size: SizeOfBuffer - 1
  64:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  65:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff == RdOff:       Buffer is empty
  66:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff == (RdOff - 1): Buffer is full
  67:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff >  RdOff:       Free space includes wrap-around
  68:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff <  RdOff:       Used space includes wrap-around
  69:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           (WrOff == (SizeOfBuffer - 1)) && (RdOff == 0):
  70:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c ****                                 Buffer full and wrap-around after next byte
  71:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  72:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  73:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  74:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
  75:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
