 730:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 731:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 732:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_ReadUpBuffer
 733:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 734:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 735:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Reads characters from SEGGER real-time-terminal control block
 736:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    which have been previously stored by the application.
 737:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Used to do the same operation that J-Link does, to transfer
 738:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    RTT data via other channels, such as TCP/IP or UART.
 739:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 740:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 741:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of Up-buffer to be used.
 742:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to buffer provided by target application, to copy characters from RTT-up-
 743:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferSize   Size of the target application buffer.
 744:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 745:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 746:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes that have been read.
 747:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 748:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
 749:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function must not be called when J-Link might also do RTT.
 750:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function locks against all other RTT operations. I.e. during
 751:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    the read operation, writing is also locked.
 752:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    If only one consumer reads from the up buffer,
 753:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    call sEGGER_RTT_ReadUpBufferNoLock() instead.
 754:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
