 804:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 805:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock
 806:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 807:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 808:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 809:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block.
 810:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock does not lock the application
 811:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and overwrites data if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 812:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 813:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 814:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 815:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 816:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 817:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 818:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 819:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, data is overwritten.
 820:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 821:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 822:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 823:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (3) Do not use SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock if a J-Link
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccZ5iSyA.s 			page 38


 824:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        connection reads RTT data.
 825:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
