1071:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1072:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteNoLock
1073:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1074:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1075:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
1076:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block which is then read by the host.
1077:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteNoLock does not lock the application.
1078:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1079:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1080:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1081:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
1082:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
1083:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1084:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1085:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1086:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1087:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccZ5iSyA.s 			page 50


1088:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) Data is stored according to buffer flags.
1089:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1090:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1091:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1092:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
