1238:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1239:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1240:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a single character/byte in SEGGER RTT buffer.
1241:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_PutCharSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
1242:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips the byte, if it does not fit into the buffer.
1243:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1244:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1245:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1246:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    c            Byte to be stored.
1247:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1248:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1249:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1250:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1251:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1252:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, the character is dropped.
1253:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1254:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1255:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1256:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
