1642:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Run-time configuration of a specific up-buffer (T->H).
1643:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Buffer to be configured is specified by index.
1644:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This includes: Buffer address, size, name, flags, ...
1645:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1646:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1647:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of the buffer to configure.
1648:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    sName        Pointer to a constant name string.
1649:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to a buffer to be used.
1650:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferSize   Size of the buffer.
1651:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Flags        Operating modes. Define behavior if buffer is full (not enough space for entire m
1652:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *                 Flags[31:24] are used for validity check and must be zero. Flags[23:2] are reserv
1653:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1654:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1655:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    >= 0 - O.K.
1656:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *     < 0 - Error
1657:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1658:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
1659:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Buffer 0 is configured on compile-time.
1660:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    May only be called once per buffer.
1661:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Buffer name and flags can be reconfigured using the appropriate functions.
1662:./trace/SEGGER/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
